<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The minimum entitlements for Electron's hardened runtime.

  The four keys below are NOT there just to be safe — with any one missing, macOS kills the app right
  at launch, and the message only says "quit unexpectedly":

    allow-jit + allow-unsigned-executable-memory  V8 compiles JavaScript to machine code at run time.
                                                   Hardened runtime forbids that by default.
    allow-dyld-environment-variables               Electron uses DYLD_* to load its frameworks.
    disable-library-validation                     Electron's frameworks are signed by Electron,
                                                   not by our Developer ID.

  Add nothing beyond these four. Every extra entitlement is one the app does not need but that someone
  who takes over the process can use.

  One more, for a feature, not for startup: device.audio-input lets the page record when the person
  presses the chat box's microphone (voice input, 15/10/2026). Without it hardened runtime refuses
  the microphone silently: no prompt, no sound. macOS still asks the person once, in the words of
  NSMicrophoneUsageDescription (build/package.sh).

  And personal-information.location: Website Opportunities' "Use my location" (18/10/2026). Without it
  hardened runtime refuses geolocation silently; macOS asks once in the words of NSLocationUsageDescription.
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.personal-information.location</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
